---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About calenda11y" nav="about" crumbLabel="About">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>About calenda11y</h1>
    <p class="lede">One place to find accessibility events, wherever you are.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <p>
      calenda11y lists conferences, meetups, workshops and talks about digital <abbr title="accessibility">a11y</abbr>:
      making websites, apps and documents work for disabled people.
    </p>
    <h2>Where the events come from</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can <a href="/submit">add an event</a>. We also collect events from the public calendars of groups that run
      accessibility events. A person checks every event before it appears, so the list stays useful and free of spam.
    </p>
    <h2>How to use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Filter events by country, format, date, price and access provisions.</li>
      <li>Add a single event to your calendar, or subscribe so new events appear on their own.</li>
      <li>Get a weekly or monthly email of events, or an email when events are added or changed.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Who pays for it</h2>
    <p>
      calenda11y is free to use and has no adverts. <a href="/sponsor">Sponsors</a> pay for hosting and moderation.
      Sponsors never get special places in the list of events.
    </p>
    <h2>Open data and open source</h2>
    <p>
      The event data is free to reuse under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence. The code is open source under
      the MIT licence, on <a href="https://github.com/camilopires/calenda11y">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
